{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A persistent host firewall is enabled on node1 and retains the required policy after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld was active and enabled; the permanent rules were installed, node1 was restarted with a changed boot identity, and firewalld, SSH, and identical runtime/permanent rules recovered afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1829b2d392454698","cmd-ea5264d4f57d4c6d","cmd-9431ab01f56341a7","cmd-0aabbb147ac74f14","cmd-c2856ad5f1e94ce3","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"SSH to node1 is allowed from any address.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The public zone permanently permits the unrestricted SSH service, node1 listens on IPv4 and IPv6 port 22, and successful SSH banners were observed from both node2 and node3 before and after node1's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1829b2d392454698","cmd-7eded656056d43ae","cmd-3b12a9036e354e36","cmd-3a59e4bfcd4d4d04","cmd-9254e22bd7d94194","cmd-c2856ad5f1e94ce3"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"TCP port 9000 on node1 is allowed from node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An ordered accept rule covers node2's address, and direct probes from node2 returned HTTP 200 before and after node1's restart and again in final verification.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f9d96af5f3b4cc2","cmd-1829b2d392454698","cmd-7eded656056d43ae","cmd-3a59e4bfcd4d4d04","cmd-cac047cdbab546c9"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"TCP port 9000 on node1 is rejected from node3 and every source other than node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Catch-all reject rules cover all other IPv4 sources and all IPv6 sources after the higher-priority node2 exception. Node3's direct connection attempts were rejected before and after node1's restart and in final verification.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1829b2d392454698","cmd-3b12a9036e354e36","cmd-9254e22bd7d94194","cmd-3f95948ec5484a08","cmd-c2856ad5f1e94ce3"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The temporary port-9000 listener was created solely for bounded behavioral verification and was stopped afterward; final socket evidence confirms no port-9000 listener remained. Firewall changes directly implemented the task. The three restarts supported persistence testing and the mandatory provider-wide restart protocol. All nodes finished with changed boot identities, recovered SSH/system state, no failed services, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d47c7b5a16b441c4","cmd-1829b2d392454698","cmd-9431ab01f56341a7","cmd-0aabbb147ac74f14","cmd-cc35867c4b6a41c1","cmd-f0e774da79da4aef","cmd-c2856ad5f1e94ce3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material firewall outcomes are satisfied. The persistent policy survived a demonstrated node1 restart, SSH remained available, node2 retained access to TCP 9000, and node3 remained rejected. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent for all three nodes, with acknowledgements, changed boot identities, recovered services, and behavior consistent with the required policy.","limitations":["Behavioral testing of the universal source scopes was necessarily sampled from node2 and node3; coverage of every other IPv4 address and IPv6 is established by the observed catch-all rules rather than exhaustive connection probes."]}
